# SUPERSEDED 2026-08-30, kept as a record. A data-driven suite runner that reflects over a call's
# children (`read call/nest`), which the language does not expose and deliberately will not: code is not
# data at run time. The live test story is `code/test.tree` (case / run / want / deny) plus `test` blocks
# executed by `term test`. The table sketches this was meant to drive are in hold/integer/, their
# portable vectors ported to deck/seed/test/integer-32.tree as ordinary test blocks.
note draft

task test-suite
  take suite
  take scope

  walk list, read suite
    hook next
      take call
      walk list, read call/nest
        hook next
          take t, name test
          fork case, read t/nest/size
            case 2
              test {scope}-{call/name}-{t/name}
                call fork/{call/name}
                  read call/a
                  read call/r
            case 3
              test {scope}-{call/name}-{t/name}
                call fork/{call/name}
                  read call/a
                  read call/b
                  read call/r